{"name":"Washed in Light","hex":"#fae8c8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"washed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of wash"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Ellipsis of washed up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/washed"},{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"}],"entries":[{"title":"Washed","blocks":[{"text":"\"Washed\" is a song recorded live by the American Christian music collective Elevation Rhythm. The song was released on September 19, 2025, through Elevation Worship Records, to digital download and streaming formats. It was written by Joe L. Barnes, Joshua Holiday, Mitch Wong, and Steven Furtick, while Holiday produced. \"Washed\" peaked at number 97 on the Billboard Hot 100 and number 1 on the Hot Christian Songs chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6c/Elevation_Rhythm_Washed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washed","wikidata":"Q140133783"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_r